{
"esm": "1.3.0",
"metadata": {
 "name": "cam_radiation",
 "description": "CAM6 radiation (RRTMG) as six pointwise/law models on the column (stage 2 of the EqESM project; components/cam/src/physics/rrtmg/ of the instrumented cam6_4_212 fork, SCAM run C_JRA_t62_scam_inst, radiation steps 3..47 of run 12255018, dump site radiation, cam_rad_*.csv). CamRadState is the rrtmg_state_create state construction (rrtmg_state.F90:60-247) on the RRTMG layer axis k (1..33 top-down: the 32 CAM layers plus the extra top layer): the shared pressure/temperature edges pint_hi(k) = pint_lo(k+1), T_ifc_hi(k) = T_ifc_lo(k+1) via the edge_shift template, the pmid branch pmid(1) = 0.5*pint_hi(1), pmid(k) = 0.5*(pint_lo+pint_hi) (F90:126,140), h2ovmr = (q/(1-q))*amdw (F90:47,198) and the cfc22vmr = ccl4vmr = 0 configuration zeroing (F90:222-223). CamRadSolin is the top-of-atmosphere incident solar flux solin = sum_b sfac_b*solar_band_irrad_b * eccf * coszrs (radsw.F90:395-397; the solar band irradiances of radconstants.F90:34-40, sum 1368.22 W/m2, are parameter defaults). CamRadSolverInputs derives the two-stream solver inputs from the in-cloud optics (radsw.F90:437-475): ssa = tau_w/tau when tau > 0 else 1, asm = tau_w_g/tau_w and fsfc = tau_w_f/tau_w when tau_w > 0 else 0 (the guarded_ratio template; the Fortran's max(x,1e-80) denominators are vacuous for the dump's nonzero ratios, and the else branches pick the exact zeros/1), and cldfprime = max(cld, cldfsnow) (radiation.F90:1012-1016; cldfsnow = cld bitwise in the window so cldfprime is a copy of an input and is not pinned). CamRadMcicaSw/CamRadMcicaLw are the McICA subcolumn cloud-optics masking (mcica_subcol_gen_sw.f90:439-444, mcica_subcol_gen_lw.f90:408-416): tauc_sto = cld_sto*tau(band(gpt)), ssac_sto = cld_sto*ssa(band(gpt)) + (1-cld_sto), asmc_sto = cld_sto*asm(band(gpt)), fsfc_sto = cld_sto*fsfc(band(gpt)) with the band->gpt k-distribution maps of rrtmg_sw_init.f90:266-280 / rrtmg_lw_init.f90:308 as [gpt]-shaped parameters gathered by the band_gather template; the stochastic cld_sto is an input (deterministic RNG, permuteseed 1 SW / 150 LW, single column -- out of scope). CamRadHeating is the heating-rate law as the layer flux divergence on the esd column (radsw.F90:565-575, radlw.F90:237-245): fns = fds - fus, fnl = ful - fdl, qrs = g*D(fns) and qrl = -g*D(fnl) on the ze = -pint_hi-reversed coordinate (esd lev 1 = surface), the history scalars as index picks (fsnt = fns[NLEV+1], fsns = fns[1], flut = fus[NLEV+1], flwds = fdl[1], ...), and sw_net/lw_net as the whole-column integrals integral(qrs/g, lev, z_sfc, z_top) = fsnt - fsns / flns - flnt. Not dumped (documented gaps): the k-distribution gas-optics (the band/gpt tau, ssa, asm, fsfc inputs themselves), the two-stream radiance solves, and the o3vmr P_top decay law of rrtmg_state (o3mmr is not dumped); the night SW boundary is all-zero (radsw.F90 early return + flush zero-fill) and is never pinned. The lev axis of the solver-input and McICA models is the esd column axis (lev 1 = surface = CAM lev 32; the dump rows are reversed in the tests). EarthSciModels' rrtm_lw is WRF RRTM (g = 9.8066, cp = 1.004, SECANG = 1.66) with deliberately different constants and is not reused (see README-cam-radiation.md).",
 "license": "MIT",
 "tags": ["stage2", "cam", "radiation", "rrtmg", "dump-pinned", "esd:column_nonuniform_1d"]
 },
"index_sets": {
 "lev": {"kind": "interval", "size": "NLEV"},
 "lev_nodes": {"kind": "interval", "size": {"op": "+", "args": ["NLEV", 1]}},
 "k": {"kind": "interval", "size": "NK"},
 "band": {"kind": "interval", "size": "NBND"},
 "gpt": {"kind": "interval", "size": "NGPT"},
 "band_lw": {"kind": "interval", "size": "NBNDL"},
 "gpt_lw": {"kind": "interval", "size": "NGPTL"}
 },
"metaparameters": {
 "NLEV": {"type": "integer", "default": 32, "description": "Number of CAM model layers (pver = 32); the esd column axis lev (1 = surface) and its NLEV+1 interfaces lev_nodes."},
 "NK": {"type": "integer", "default": 33, "description": "Number of RRTMG layers of the state construction (rrtmg_state.F90:64): the 32 CAM layers plus the extra top layer, k = 1..33 top-down (dump order, no reversal)."},
 "NBND": {"type": "integer", "default": 14, "description": "Number of RRTMG shortwave bands (nbndsw = 14)."},
 "NGPT": {"type": "integer", "default": 112, "description": "Number of RRTMG shortwave g-points (ngptsw = 112)."},
 "NBNDL": {"type": "integer", "default": 16, "description": "Number of RRTMG longwave bands (nbndlw = 16)."},
 "NGPTL": {"type": "integer", "default": 140, "description": "Number of RRTMG longwave g-points (ngptlw = 140)."}
 },
