  "tests": [
   {
    "id": "step37",
    "description": "cam_rad_solver_sw.csv rows (step 37, day, thin cloud cld ~ 0.12, gpt x lev) joined to the cam_rad_cldopt_sw.csv band optics: the McICA subcolumn masking of mcica_subcol_gen_sw.f90:439-444 - tauc_sto = cld_sto*tau(band(gpt)), ssac_sto = cld_sto*ssa(band(gpt)) + (1-cld_sto), asmc_sto = cld_sto*asm(band(gpt)), fsfc_sto = cld_sto*fsfc(band(gpt)) - with band(gpt) the SW k-distribution map (rrtmg_sw_init.f90:266-280, counts 6,12,8,8,10,10,2,10,8,6,6,8,6,12). The stochastic cld_sto itself is an input: it is generated by the deterministic RNG of mcica_subcol_gen_sw.f90 (permuteseed = 1, single column), which is out of scope. Pinned at the first cloudy subcolumns of bands 2, 6, 14 at the cloudy level (CAM lev 15 = esd lev 18) and the cld_sto = 0 fill branch (ssac_sto = 1).",
